      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, looking at ticket #88291—the customer is claiming their ceramic vase arrived shattered and is demanding a full refund. I know the shipping carrier logs usually tell us if there was a high-impact event during transit, but this one looks inconclusive. Based on the carrier data and the customer's claim, what's the most efficient way to handle this so we don't lose the customer but also minimize unnecessary costs?",
